OF Arena can host any type of inventory or questionnaire data. A typical process when working with Arena
will be as follows:

●  Log in to the platform;

●  Select a survey;

●  Depending on the user role: view, input, validate, edit, or export data;

●  Data analysis with the help of R scripts [roles: Survey Administrator, Data Analyst],

●  View and export the results and reports;

●  Log out from the platform.

To open your user profile, click on your profile picture in the top-right corner and select My profile.

In your user profile you can:

•  add a profile picture: drop an image or click Upload, then adjust it with Scale and Rotate;

•  set your Title and Name (your email address is your login and cannot be changed here);

•  view the Extra properties assigned to you (see 6.1.4);

•  type your own API key for Planet basemaps in Map API Keys (click Test to check it);

•  change your password with Change password (see Chapter 13).

Click Save to save your changes.

System administrators also find here the Notification preferences (e.g. receive an email for New user
access requests) and the Manage 2FA button (see 3.4).

In the case of a multi-cycle survey, a Data Analyst (or a user with a higher role) can clone records from one
cycle to another. The following conditions apply:

●  The survey should contain more than 1 cycle;
●  The survey must be published;
●  Only data from older cycle can be cloned to newer, i.e. from Cycle 1 to 2, or from Cycle 2 to 3, but
not backwards;
●  Records cannot be overwritten in the target cycle; already existing records are skipped;
●  Record key attribute definitions, defined on the Form Designer, must be the same in source and
target cycle; if they have been modified, cloning will not work;
●  The Clone-button is not shown on the last cycle’s record list;

When you want to clone data, do as follows:

1) Select the source cycle in the cycle selector at the top of the page, e.g.

2) Select the records to be cloned

If you want to clone all records, you do not need to make any selection.

3) Click on
4) Select the target cycle (To cycle); only later cycles can be selected,
5) Select whether you want to clone all records or only the selected ones:

6) Click on Start cloning and confirm. When cloning is complete, a message shows how many records
were cloned.

Always before using data import in Arena, take a backup of your survey with data. Read more here.

Arena can import external data from

1) CSV or Excel files;
2) Open Foris Collect / Collect Mobile files;
3) Arena (backup) / Arena Mobile (export) files;

A survey should be published before a data import is possible.

If you are adding new information into the database using CSV or Excel files, import your data by following a
top-down method! In the case of the survey structure described in the next chapter, first enter CLUSTER data

as new records, then PLOT data with "update existing records", and then similarly "Reference objects", and
so on. Data import template files are numbered to make data importing a bit easier.

Users with the System administrator privilege see the System Administration menu at the bottom of the
sidebar. It is not linked to the current survey and contains the following items:

•  Users access requests: requests sent with the Request access link of the login page (shown only when
access requests are enabled on the server);

•  Users list (all): all the users of the server, with Export to Excel, Backup / Restore and New User;

•  Job monitor: the background jobs (imports, exports, publishing...) of all users; select Active jobs only
to see the running jobs, and cancel a job if needed;

•  System Logs: the server log, live;

•  Messages: messages sent to the users by email or as in-app notifications.

System administrators also see the Changelog in the Help menu.

In Messages, click New to write a message:

•  Subject and Body: the body can be formatted with Markdown and can contain the placeholders
{{userTitleAndName}} and {{userName}}; switch on Preview to see the result;

•  Notification Type: Email, In App Notification or both;

•  Target User Type: All Users, or only some types of users, e.g. Survey Administrators (to write only
to the administrators of the surveys) or Individual Users (type their email addresses in Included
Emails); use Excluded Emails to leave out some users;

•  Date Valid Until: until when the in-app notification is shown.

Click Send Message. The message is sent in the background and a progress dialog is shown: you can cancel
the sending from it. Messages already sent are not recalled.
